ors are semantic tokens ({scheme}-{weight}), never hex/rgb. background also accepts surface | overlay | page | transparent.","layout.defaults":"Never write props equal to defaults or implied by another prop on the element: position=\"relative\", direction on Row/Column, variant=\"primary\" on Button, fillWidth beside maxWidth (maxWidth already fills the width), minWidth={0} beside fillWidth (fillWidth already sets min-width: 0).","Select.closed":"Fixed in 2.1: Select closes on pick and stays closed — focus returning to the field no longer reopens it — and a multiple Select stays open while picking. Use Select with value and onSelect; do not build a local picker from DropdownWrapper and Options to get this.","NumberInput.value":"Fixed in 2.1: NumberInput follows its value prop after mount (an undo, a reset, a change made elsewhere) without rewriting what the user is typing. Pass value and onChange; do not remount it with a key to push a new value in.","layout.responsiveProps":"Responsive xl/l/m/s/xs props exist only on Flex, Row, Column and Grid. Button, Text, Heading and the rest have none: to change one at a breakpoint, wrap it in a Row or Column and put the breakpoint prop there (s={{ hide: true }}). Text and Heading take padding and flex but no radius or border; put those on the wrapper.","size.rem":"A number on width, height, minWidth or minHeight is rem, not px: width={32} is 512 px. For a pixel size write the spacing token string, width=\"32\" (32 px), or the rem value, width={2}. Token strings stop at the spacing scale (\"160\" is the largest), so height=\"320\" is a type error: write height={20}. An icon or avatar box is usually \"24\" to \"48\".","spacing.tokens":"gap, padding and margin take spacing tokens (\"0\", \"1\", \"2\", \"4\", \"8\", \"12\", \"16\", \"20\", \"24\", \"32\", \"40\", \"48\", \"56\", \"64\", \"72\", \"80\", \"104\", \"128\", \"160\", or xs–xl). \"6\" and \"10\" are not tokens and are type errors.","layout.noSpanOrType":"Row, Column and Grid have no span and no type prop. A clickable row is a Button (or a native <button>), and a Grid child spanning columns uses style={{ gridColumn: \"span 2\" }}.","Column.form":"Wrap a Column in a native <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>. Column as=\"form\" keeps the div event types, so a FormEvent<HTMLFormElement> handler (and noValidate) is a type error.","Checkbox.checked":"Checkbox, Switch and RadioButton take checked (or defaultChecked) and onToggle(checked: boolean). isChecked and isIndeterminate were 1.x; the 2.x props are checked and indeterminate."},"quality":{"sectionNav":"Tabs orientation=\"vertical\" with s={{ direction: \"column\" }} (and the TabList s={{ direction: \"row\" }}), one TabPanel per section, keepMounted on a form panel. Sections that are routes use NavItem href instead","settingRow":"One Setting per control — label and description left, control right. A list of Settings needs no surface around it","grouping":"SettingGroup with a header control and open={enabled}, so sub-settings sit inside its box; SettingAxes for X/Y pairs","explainers":"info on a Setting (an InfoTip) instead of a description line that is only needed once","forms":"Profile fields in a Form (columns per breakpoint), not hand-spaced Columns","surfaceRecipe":"background=\"surface\" border radius=\"l\" padding=\"24\"","dangerZone":"border=\"danger-alpha-medium\" on danger actions only"},"mixins":{"CommonProps":{"onBackground":"Colors","onSolid":"Colors","align":"CSSProperties[\"textAlign\"]"},"DisplayProps":{"as":"ElementType","inline":"boolean","hide":"boolean","pointerEvents":"\"none\" | \"all\" | \"auto\"","userSelect":"UserSelect","position":"CSSProperties[\"position\"]","overflow":"CSSProperties[\"overflow\"]","overflowX":"CSSProperties[\"overflowX\"]","overflowY":"CSSProperties[\"overflowY\"]","scrollbar":"\"default\" | \"minimal\"","transition":"\"micro-short\" | \"micro-medium\" | \"micro-long\" | \"macro-short\" | \"macro-medium\" | \"macro-long\"","opacity":"Opacity",